            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0580" n="500" xml:id="pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Canada/4337</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Riggs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-04">June 4, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received June 9.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1443</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my despatch No. 1430 of
                    May 23, 1930,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d545-f1"/> and as a conclusion to that and to
                    the series of previous despatches regarding the debate in the Canadian
                    Parliament on Bill No. 15, entitled “An Act to Amend the Export Act”, I have the
                    honor to report that this Bill received the Royal assent, and consequently
                    became law, at the final session of Parliament on May 30, 1930.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. Reath Riggs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
